{"agent":"lane-wf-lanes-roster","data":{"budget":"","claim":"A free lane silent for ghost_after_s is only history; classing it gone, leaving it out of the default table with a footer count and cutting the table at output.max_rows turns the 103-row listing of 100 ghosts and 3 live lanes into 3 rows plus a footer.","falsifier":"On the unfixed code the new test expecting 3 shown rows and a footer for 100 ghosts (last event 20 h old) plus 3 live lanes passes, or the fixed code still lists 103 rows.","item":"WF-lanes-roster-cap","mechanism":"ledger._free gave IDLE_READY to every lane without a recorded end whenever any ready item existed, and build() listed every lane inside the 24 h window, so session starts without ends (256 starts, 20 ends) stayed listed as idle-with-ready-work.","probe":"uv run pytest -q tests/test_lanes_ghost_ttl.py (on the unfixed code, before the change)","probe_output":"7 failed, 1 passed: test_a_free_lane_silent_past_the_ttl_is_gone_not_idle_with_ready_work, test_default_table_has_the_live_rows_and_a_gone_footer, test_all_lists_every_lane_up_to_the_row_cap, test_the_table_obeys_output_max_rows_and_says_how_many_more, test_idle_with_ready_work_needs_an_event_inside_idle_s, test_the_cut_keeps_working_lanes_before_idle_ones, test_cli_and_json_leave_the_ghost_out_and_all_brings_it_back all failed. After the change: 9 passed.","question":"Why is ddflow lanes 34 KB, and does a ghost TTL plus row cap fix it?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"ef3fda555534b037759136308","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":195804,"schema":1,"subject":"R-lanes-roster-cap","ts":"2026-11-13T19:07:34.901587Z"}
