{"agent":"lane-wf-lanes-roster","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"`_is_ghost` computes silence from `last_event` only (`now - last`), while `_free` immediately computes `quiet` from `max(last_event, heartbeat)` and `_heard_from` treats a heartbeat as proof the lane is heard from. Given `[lanes].ghost_after_s=7200`, `[lanes].idle_s=900`, `now=100000.0`, a free lane with `last_event=92000.0` (8000 s old), `heartbeat=99500.0` (500 s old), and any ready work: `_free` sets `quiet=500.0`, so `_heard_from` would be true, but `_is_ghost` returns true because `8000.0 >= 7200`, so `_free` returns `Lane(state=S.GONE, ...)`. The lane is hidden/counted as gone despite a fresh heartbeat, preventing it from being shown as idle-ready or used by advise.","digest":"f1d3f515f58c8b12","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/ledger.py:_is_ghost","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/ledger.py:_is_ghost"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The footer text can tell the user that `--all` will list lanes even when `[output].allow_full` is false. `_row_cap` sets `refused = show_all` when `allow_full` is false, so in the default view (`show_all=False`) `refused` is always false; the `more` note then prints “everything: `ddflow lanes --all` …”. The `gone` note always prints “`ddflow lanes --all` … lists them” without checking `allow_full` at all. Given `[output] allow_full=false`, `max_rows=10`, and 20 non-gone lanes (or 100 gone lanes), `select_roster` emits a footer promising that `--all` lists everything, but calling `select_roster(..., show_all=True)` still applies the 10-row cap and omits lanes. This contradicts the intended behavior that `--all` lifts the cap only when `allow_full` is true.","digest":"fd63d36673633538","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/roster.py:72-79","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/roster.py:72-79"}],"chunks_total":8,"coverage":"8/8 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":33042,"diff_sha":"cb449965b83190d6d7d8279944c605df6690b981c243cda44f27de14456590a7","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/WF-lanes-roster-cap","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":807.8,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"5c4407bc9257107d","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/WF-lanes-roster-cap.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T190925Z-db4fccd7.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],"reviewed_head":"631437f86d32ad80196fe2db14e3074770a3f2df","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/lane_views.py":"100644 d86281a928180988b228da7c71a1bf4ef7e862f4","ddflow/config_sections/lanes.py":"100644 9a0870f340f09618fe8a459d051c609ad58b89a9","ddflow/services/fleet.py":"100644 99ebd9ffeb47429597e29450f6507300a5000b01","ddflow/services/lanes/__init__.py":"100644 1068ae022d534e21223ae93c9d8de81ec4ef2e78","ddflow/services/lanes/lead.py":"100644 5f3bcbd37860e0776192ad20921e7cbb6ccf5014","ddflow/services/lanes/ledger.py":"100644 658761833cc253417fd307c8e0b71354c075da18","ddflow/services/lanes/render.py":"100644 8a88db5c0d91aca86e4f180014a25fe88d7a5e00","ddflow/services/lanes/roster.py":"100644 f1c3dc6409284b55258aac40222e5f38e8534474","ddflow/services/lanes/states.py":"100644 a22501c8e16eaa5c37c5a164669218bc1d001744","ddflow/surfaces/declared/lanes.py":"100644 568229da59f2ea96d9334e6704fc755ecdd0031a","ddflow/templates/prompts/help/lanes.md":"100644 8e64e3145dff8d4cac1d3331152c7b652c5535de","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.lanes.ghost_after_s.toml":"100644 53028a451d5bddc978f1804336944dbfa24e3d0a","docs/ddflow/drivers/deltas/fleet-registry.md":"100644 8d496f53e1b5e9a89548e5b68e0ed67a27b78735","docs/guide/parallelism.md":"100644 1ba554db24775a0883572d9bca054d4f96952f37","tests/lanes_fi