{"agent":"lane-wf-lanes-roster","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":4,"detail":"The footer promises that `ddflow lanes --all` will list omitted lanes even when `[output].allow_full = false` prevents `--all` from lifting the row cap. `_row_cap` sets `refused = show_all`, so for the default table (`show_all=False`) `refused` is false even though `--all` would be refused; the “more” footer then says “everything: `ddflow lanes --all`”. The “gone” footer also unconditionally says `--all` lists the gone lanes. Concrete: with `cfg.output.allow_full=False`, `cfg.output.max_rows=10`, and 15 non-gone lanes, `select_roster(..., show_all=False)` returns a footer saying the 5 omitted lanes can be seen with `--all`, but `select_roster(..., show_all=True)` with the same config returns only 10 shown and 5 more, so `--all` does not list everything. The same mismatch applies to gone lanes: with 100 gone lanes and 10 non-gone lanes, the default footer says `--all` lists the 100 gone lanes, while `--all` keeps the 10 non-gone lanes first and cuts all gone lanes.","digest":"7f19c807d119506d","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/roster.py:select_roster/_row_cap","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/roster.py:select_roster/_row_cap"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The new `--all` help line says `ddflow lanes --all` lists every lane “past the `[output].max_rows` row cap”, but the same section says the table is cut at `[output].max_rows` with an `N more` footer, and the new upgrade record says the table is cut at `[output].max_rows`. Given `[output].max_rows = 10` and 100 lanes, the help promises that `ddflow lanes --all` / `ddflow_lanes all=true` prints all 100 rows; if the implementation follows that, the newly added row cap can be bypassed and the command can still emit the full 147-line roster, defeating the stated bounded-output goal. If the implementation follows the cap, the new `--all` documentation is false.","digest":"7bfb5b33ef98f410","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/templates/prompts/help/lanes.md:8","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/templates/prompts/help/lanes.md:8"}],"chunks_total":8,"coverage":"8/8 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":33042,"diff_sha":"cb449965b83190d6d7d8279944c605df6690b981c243cda44f27de14456590a7","diff_source":"73d7cecdb129a567dca22226402a0807a233da01..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/WF-lanes-roster-cap (WARNING: main was history-rewritten since the item forked from 73d7cecdb129: the reviewer sees only the item's own commits on top of that recorded base)","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":777.1,"excluded_bytes":1453,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["README.md","ddflow/templates/default.toml"],"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"094a915147131795","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/WF-lanes-roster-cap.critic.[REDACTED:name].20261113T192313Z-3df53f6d.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794598571.2304187,"family":"xai","gate":"critic","model":"grok-4.7","reason":"HTTP 403","reviewer":"grok-4.7"}],"review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],"reviewed_head":"631437f86d32ad80196fe2db14e3074770a3f2df","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/lane_views.py":"100644 d86281a928180988b228da7c71a1bf4ef7e862f4","ddflow/config_sections/lanes.py":"100644 9a0870f340f09618fe8a459d051c609ad58b89a9","ddflow/services/fleet.py":"100644 99ebd9ffeb47429597e29450f6507300a5000b01","ddflow/services/lanes/__init__.py":"100644 1068ae022d534e21223ae93c9d8de81ec4ef2e78","ddflow/services/lanes/lead.py":"100644 5f3bcbd37860e0776192ad20921e7cbb6ccf5014","ddflow/services/lanes/ledger.py":"100644 658761833cc253417fd307c8e0b71354c075da18","ddflow/services/lanes/render.py":"100644 8a88db5c0d91aca86e4f180014a25fe88d7a5e00","ddf