{"agent":"lane-wf-lanes-roster","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":4,"detail":"The footer promises that `ddflow lanes --all` will list omitted lanes even when `[output].allow_full = false` prevents `--all` from lifting the row cap. `_row_cap` sets `refused = show_all`, so for the default table (`show_all=False`) `refused` is false even though `--all` would be refused; the “more” footer then says “everything: `ddflow lanes --all`”. The “gone” footer also unconditionally says `--all` lists the gone lanes. Concrete: with `cfg.output.allow_full=False`, `cfg.output.max_rows=10`, and 15 non-gone lanes, `select_roster(..., show_all=False)` returns a footer saying the 5 omitted lanes can be seen with `--all`, but `select_roster(..., show_all=True)` with the same config returns only 10 shown and 5 more, so `--all` does not list everything. The same mismatch applies to gone lanes: with 100 gone lanes and 10 non-gone lanes, the default footer says `--all` lists the 100 gone lanes, while `--all` keeps the 10 non-gone lanes first and cuts all gone lanes.","digest":"7f19c807d119506d","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/roster.py:select_roster/_row_cap","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/roster.py:select_roster/_row_cap"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The new `--all` help line says `ddflow lanes --all` lists every lane “past the `[output].max_rows` row cap”, but the same section says the table is cut at `[output].max_rows` with an `N more` footer, and the new upgrade record says the table is cut at `[output].max_rows`. Given `[output].max_rows = 10` and 100 lanes, the help promises that `ddflow lanes --all` / `ddflow_lanes all=true` prints all 100 rows; if the implementation follows that, the newly added row cap can be bypassed and the command can still emit the full 147-line roster, defeating the stated bounded-output goal. If the implementation follows the cap, the 